IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa11-part16-ch1.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 16 (Audit), Chapter 1 (Requirement for audited accounts),
-- ss 475 to 484: raw lines 6543-6697 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.  LAYER 1: the law, objectively; no seat, no point of view.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the official text
-- and nothing here is "verified against the official text".  Quote lines are checked against that rendering by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md "Reading a result").
--   JUST TRUE   the text says the case is within what the function's name asks.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words ("means", "if", "only if", "unless", "where", a flat negative).
--               Each such branch carries   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<the quoted words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide (silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the text,
--               limited by its own wording).  Each such branch carries   -- NOTHING-kind (<why>)
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- THE POLARITY OF EACH NAME.  A function named "... is barred ..." or "... is not entitled ... for want of ..." is a BAR:
--   JUST TRUE = barred, JUST FALSE = the text says the bar does not catch this case.  A function named "... is exempt ..."
--   or "... is entitled to the exemption ..." is an EXEMPTION: JUST TRUE = exempt, JUST FALSE = "this section gives no
--   exemption on these facts" (never "no exemption at all"; ruling of 2026-11-05, NOTHINGBURGER (b), applied by analogy:
--   fork F1 in NOTES.md).
-- INPUTS.  An answer another part computes (PLAN.md section 4) is an input named for its section, MAYBE BOOLEAN where
--   the keel or another part may answer NOTHING, so that NOTHING stays NOTHING.  A fact the person can state is BOOLEAN.
--   A percentage is a NUMBER fraction (10% is 0.1).  A date is `Date day month year`.
-- Every top-level name, type, constructor and field begins with the label of the provision it implements.

§ `Part 16 Chapter 1: Requirement for audited accounts (ss 475 to 484)`

§§ `s 475 Requirement for audited accounts`

-- The four exemptions s 475(1) lists, so that "any such exemption" (s 475(2)) and "any of the provisions mentioned in
-- subsection (1)(a)" (s 475(3)) can be told apart.
-- src:6547 | (1) A company's annual accounts for a financial year must be audited in accordance with this Part unless the company—
-- src:6548 | (a) is exempt from audit under—
-- src:6549 | section 477 (small companies),
-- src:6550 | section 479A (subsidiary companies) or
-- src:6551 | section 480 (dormant companies);
-- src:6552 | or
-- src:6553 | (b) is exempt from the requirements of this Part under section 482 (non-profit-making companies subject to public sector audit).
@ref s 475(1) Requirement for audited accounts (the four exemptions) (src:6547-6553)
DECLARE `s 475 exemption` IS ONE OF
    `s 475 the small companies exemption (section 477)`
    `s 475 the subsidiary companies exemption (section 479A)`
    `s 475 the dormant companies exemption (section 480)`
    `s 475 the public sector audit exemption (section 482)`

-- src:6547 | (1) A company's annual accounts for a financial year must be audited in accordance with this Part unless the company—
-- src:6548 | (a) is exempt from audit under—
-- src:6549 | section 477 (small companies),
-- src:6550 | section 479A (subsidiary companies) or
-- src:6551 | section 480 (dormant companies);
-- src:6552 | or
-- src:6553 | (b) is exempt from the requirements of this Part under section 482 (non-profit-making companies subject to public sector audit).
@ref s 475(1) Requirement for audited accounts (src:6547-6553)
GIVEN `exempt from audit under section 477 (small companies)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `exempt from audit under section 479A (subsidiary companies)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `exempt from audit under section 480 (dormant companies)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `exempt from the requirements of Part 16 under section 482 (non-profit-making companies subject to public sector audit)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 475(1) the company's annual accounts for the financial year must be audited in accordance with Part 16` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF    `exempt from audit under section 477 (small companies)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `exempt from audit under section 479A (subsidiary companies)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `exempt from audit under section 480 (dormant companies)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `exempt from the requirements of Part 16 under section 482 (non-profit-making companies subject to public sector audit)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be audited in accordance with this Part unless the company"
        IF    `exempt from audit under section 477 (small companies)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
          AND `exempt from audit under section 479A (subsidiary companies)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
          AND `exempt from audit under section 480 (dormant companies)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
          AND `exempt from the requirements of Part 16 under section 482 (non-profit-making companies subject to public sector audit)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST TRUE -- no exemption applies: the main rule stands ("must be audited ... unless")
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an exemption answer is not known (it rests on section 382, 383, 384, 474 or another part's answer)

-- s 475(2) is printed twice in the text, with different words and no mark of which is in force (finding 1, fork F2).
-- Both printed versions are encoded; the seat takes a position only where the two agree.
-- src:6554 | (2) A company is not entitled to any such exemption unless its balance sheet contains a statement by the directors to that effect.
@ref s 475(2) first printed version (src:6554-6554)
GIVEN `the balance sheet contains a statement by the directors to the effect that the company is entitled to the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 475(2) (first printed version) the company is barred from the exemption for want of the directors' statement` MEANS
    IF `the balance sheet contains a statement by the directors to the effect that the company is entitled to the exemption`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not entitled to any such exemption unless its balance sheet contains a statement by the directors to that effect" (the unless is met: fork F3)
    ELSE JUST TRUE -- "A company is not entitled to any such exemption unless" the statement is there

-- src:6555 | (2) A company is not entitled to any such exemption unless its balance sheet contains a statement by the directors—
-- src:6556 | (a) identifying the exemption in question, and
-- src:6557 | (b) confirming that the company qualifies for the exemption.
@ref s 475(2) second printed version (src:6555-6557)
GIVEN `the statement identifies the exemption in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement confirms that the company qualifies for the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 475(2) (second printed version) the company is barred from the exemption for want of the directors' statement` MEANS
    IF `the statement identifies the exemption in question` AND `the statement confirms that the company qualifies for the exemption`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not entitled to any such exemption unless its balance sheet contains a statement by the directors— (a) identifying the exemption in question, and (b) confirming that the company qualifies for the exemption" (the unless is met: fork F3)
    ELSE JUST TRUE -- "A company is not entitled to any such exemption unless" both limbs are met

-- src:6558 | (3) A company is not entitled to exemption under any of the provisions mentioned in subsection (1)(a) unless its balance sheet contains a statement by the directors to the effect that—
-- src:6559 | (a) the members have not required the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year in question in accordance with section 476, and
-- src:6560 | (b) the directors acknowledge their responsibilities for complying with the requirements of this Act with respect to accounting records and the preparation of accounts.
@ref s 475(3) Statements that the members have not required an audit and that the directors acknowledge their responsibilities (src:6558-6560)
GIVEN exemption IS A `s 475 exemption`
      `the statement says that the members have not required the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year in accordance with section 476` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement says that the directors acknowledge their responsibilities for complying with the requirements of this Act with respect to accounting records and the preparation of accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 475(3) the company is barred from the exemption for want of the directors' statements` MEANS
    CONSIDER exemption
    WHEN `s 475 the public sector audit exemption (section 482)` THEN
        NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "exemption under any of the provisions mentioned in subsection (1)(a)" does not include section 482, which is mentioned in subsection (1)(b)
    OTHERWISE
        IF    `the statement says that the members have not required the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year in accordance with section 476`
          AND `the statement says that the directors acknowledge their responsibilities for complying with the requirements of this Act with respect to accounting records and the preparation of accounts`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not entitled to exemption under any of the provisions mentioned in subsection (1)(a) unless its balance sheet contains a statement by the directors to the effect that" (the unless is met: fork F3)
        ELSE JUST TRUE -- "not entitled ... unless" both statements are there

-- src:6561 | (4) The statement required by subsection (2) or (3) must appear on the balance sheet above the signature required by section 414.
@ref s 475(4) Where the statement must appear (src:6561-6561)
GIVEN `the statement appears on the balance sheet above the signature required by section 414` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 475(4) the statement appears on the balance sheet above the signature required by section 414` MEANS
    IF `the statement appears on the balance sheet above the signature required by section 414`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement required by subsection (2) or (3) must appear on the balance sheet above the signature required by section 414" (a bare must not done: fork F4)

-- The shared rule that sections 477(5), 479A(3), 480(3) and 482(4) each state for their own exemption ("has effect subject
-- to ..."): an exemption is in force only if its own conditions hold, no bar applies, and the statement of s 475(2) and (3) is
-- on the balance sheet where s 475(4) puts it.  Each bar is in BAR polarity (JUST TRUE = barred); a members' notice under
-- s 476 is in bar polarity too (JUST TRUE = a valid notice has been given).  Fork F5 for the reading.
-- src:6554 | (2) A company is not entitled to any such exemption unless its balance sheet contains a statement by the directors to that effect.
-- src:6555 | (2) A company is not entitled to any such exemption unless its balance sheet contains a statement by the directors—
-- src:6556 | (a) identifying the exemption in question, and
-- src:6557 | (b) confirming that the company qualifies for the exemption.
-- src:6558 | (3) A company is not entitled to exemption under any of the provisions mentioned in subsection (1)(a) unless its balance sheet contains a statement by the directors to the effect that—
-- src:6559 | (a) the members have not required the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year in question in accordance with section 476, and
-- src:6560 | (b) the directors acknowledge their responsibilities for complying with the requirements of this Act with respect to accounting records and the preparation of accounts.
-- src:6561 | (4) The statement required by subsection (2) or (3) must appear on the balance sheet above the signature required by section 414.
@ref s 475(2) to (4) Statements to be contained in the balance sheet (src:6554-6561)
GIVEN `the exemption's own conditions` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      bars IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the statement placed as section 475(4) requires` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 475(2) to (4) the exemption is in force once the restrictions on it are taken together` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF    any (GIVEN bar YIELD bar EQUALS JUST TRUE) bars
           OR `the statement placed as section 475(4) requires` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is not entitled to any such exemption unless"
        IF `the exemption's own conditions` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): this section gives no exemption on these facts (fork F1)
        IF    `the exemption's own conditions` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          AND all (GIVEN bar YIELD bar EQUALS JUST FALSE) bars
          AND `the statement placed as section 475(4) requires` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer the restrictions depend on is not known

§§ `s 476 Right of members to require audit`

-- src:6564 | (2) The notice must be given by—
-- src:6565 | (a) members representing not less in total than 10% in nominal value of the company's issued share capital, or any class of it, or
-- src:6566 | (b) if the company does not have a share capital, not less than 10% in number of the members of the company.
@ref s 476(2) Who must give the notice (src:6564-6566)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fraction of the nominal value of the company's issued share capital held by the members giving the notice` IS A NUMBER
      `the largest fraction of the nominal value of any one class of the issued share capital held by the members giving the notice` IS A NUMBER
      `the fraction of the members of the company who give the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 476(2) the notice is given by enough members` MEANS
    IF `the company has a share capital`
    THEN IF    `the fraction of the nominal value of the company's issued share capital held by the members giving the notice` AT LEAST 10%
            OR `the largest fraction of the nominal value of any one class of the issued share capital held by the members giving the notice` AT LEAST 10%
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must be given by— (a) members representing not less in total than 10% in nominal value of the company's issued share capital, or any class of it" (a bare must not done: fork F4)
    ELSE IF `the fraction of the members of the company who give the notice` AT LEAST 10%
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the company does not have a share capital, not less than 10% in number of the members of the company"

-- src:6567 | (3) The notice may not be given before the financial year to which it relates and must be given not later than one month before the end of that year.
@ref s 476(3) When the notice may be given (src:6567-6567)
GIVEN `the last day of the financial year to which the notice relates` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 476(3) the last day on which the notice may be given` MEANS
    `add months` `the last day of the financial year to which the notice relates` (0 MINUS 1) -- "not later than one month before the end of that year": the same day one month earlier, capped at the end of a shorter month (fork F6)

-- src:6567 | (3) The notice may not be given before the financial year to which it relates and must be given not later than one month before the end of that year.
@ref s 476(3) When the notice may be given (src:6567-6567)
GIVEN `the first day of the financial year to which the notice relates` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the financial year to which the notice relates` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 476(3) the notice is given in time` MEANS
    IF    `the day the notice is given` AT LEAST `the first day of the financial year to which the notice relates`
      AND `the day the notice is given` AT MOST `s 476(3) the last day on which the notice may be given` `the last day of the financial year to which the notice relates`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice may not be given before the financial year to which it relates and must be given not later than one month before the end of that year"

-- src:6563 | (1) The members of a company that would otherwise be entitled to exemption from audit under any of the provisions mentioned in section 475(1)(a) may by notice under this section require it to obtain an audit of its accounts for a financial year.
@ref s 476(1) Members may require an audit by notice (src:6563-6563)
GIVEN `the company would otherwise be entitled to exemption from audit under a provision mentioned in section 475(1)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 476(2) is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 476(3) is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 476(1) the members may by notice require the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the financial year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `section 476(2) is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `section 476(3) is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must be given by" and "may not be given before the financial year to which it relates and must be given not later than one month before the end of that year" (fork F7)
        IF    `the company would otherwise be entitled to exemption from audit under a provision mentioned in section 475(1)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          AND `section 476(2) is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          AND `section 476(3) is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the company would otherwise be entitled to exemption from audit under a provision mentioned in section 475(1)(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The members of a company that would otherwise be entitled to exemption from audit under any of the provisions mentioned in section 475(1)(a) may by notice require it"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer the grant depends on is not known

§§ `s 477 Small companies: conditions for exemption from audit`

-- src:6570 | (1) A company that qualifies as a small company in relation to a financial year is exempt from the requirements of this Act relating to the audit of accounts for that year.
@ref s 477(1) Small companies are exempt; s 477(4)(a) smallness is determined by section 382 (src:6570-6570)
GIVEN `s 382 the company qualifies as a small company in relation to the financial year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 477(1) the company is exempt from audit under section 477` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 382 the company qualifies as a small company in relation to the financial year` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 382 the company qualifies as a small company in relation to the financial year` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company that qualifies as a small company in relation to a financial year is exempt" read as closed by section 475(1) ("unless the company ... is exempt from audit under section 477"): this section gives no exemption on these facts (fork F1)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a company qualifies as a small company "shall be determined in accordance with section 382(1) to (6)" (section 382 is another part's range)

-- src:6576 | (5) This section has effect subject to—
-- src:6577 | section 475(2) and (3) (requirements as to statements to be contained in balance sheet),
-- src:6578 | section 476 (right of members to require audit),
-- src:6579 | section 478 (companies excluded from small companies exemption), and
-- src:6580 | section 479 (availability of small companies exemption in case of group company).
@ref s 477(5) This section has effect subject to ... (src:6576-6580)
GIVEN `section 477(1) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 478 answer (BAR polarity)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 479 answer (BAR polarity)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 475(2) answer (BAR polarity)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 475(3) answer (BAR polarity)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 475(4) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a valid notice under section 476 has been given` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 477(5) the company is entitled to the exemption conferred by section 477` MEANS
    `s 475(2) to (4) the exemption is in force once the restrictions on it are taken together`
        `section 477(1) answer`
        (LIST `section 478 answer (BAR polarity)`, `section 479 answer (BAR polarity)`, `section 475(2) answer (BAR polarity)`, `section 475(3) answer (BAR polarity)`, `a valid notice under section 476 has been given`)
        `section 475(4) answer`

§§ `s 478 Companies excluded from small companies exemption`

-- src:6581 | 478 Companies excluded from small companies exemption
-- src:6582 | A company is not entitled to the exemption conferred by section 477 (small companies) if it was at any time within the financial year in question—
-- src:6583 | (a) a public company,
-- src:6584 | (b) a company that—
-- src:6585 | (i) is an authorised insurance company, a banking company, an e-money issuer, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company, or
-- src:6586 | (ii) carries on insurance market activity, or
-- src:6587 | (iii) is a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme within the meanings given by section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act (Northern Ireland) 2021 (interpretation of Part 1), or
-- src:6588 | (c) a special register body as defined in section 117(1) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (c. 52) or an employers' association as defined in section 122 of that Act or Article 4 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992 (S.I. 1992/807 (N.I. 5)).
@ref s 478 Companies excluded from small companies exemption (src:6581-6588)
GIVEN `was at some time within the financial year a public company (section 4(2))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was at some time within the financial year an authorised insurance company (section 1165(2))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was at some time within the financial year a banking company (section 1164(2))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 474 was at some time within the financial year an e-money issuer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 474 was at some time within the financial year a MiFID investment firm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 474 was at some time within the financial year a UCITS management company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `was at some time within the financial year carrying on insurance market activity (section 1165)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was at some time within the financial year a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme within the meanings given by section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act (Northern Ireland) 2021` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was at some time within the financial year a special register body as defined in section 117(1) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was at some time within the financial year an employers' association as defined in section 122 of that Act or Article 4 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 478 the company is barred from the small companies exemption` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN limb YIELD limb EQUALS JUST TRUE) limbs THEN JUST TRUE -- "A company is not entitled to the exemption conferred by section 477 (small companies) if it was at any time within the financial year in question"
        IF all (GIVEN limb YIELD limb EQUALS JUST FALSE) limbs
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not entitled to the exemption conferred by section 477 (small companies) if it was at any time within the financial year in question— (a) a public company, (b) a company that ..., or (c) a special register body": no listed kind holds, so this section does not bar it (fork F8)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a borrowed definition (e-money issuer, MiFID investment firm, UCITS management company: section 474(1)) is not known
    WHERE
        limbs MEANS
            LIST (JUST `was at some time within the financial year a public company (section 4(2))`)
               , (JUST `was at some time within the financial year an authorised insurance company (section 1165(2))`)
               , (JUST `was at some time within the financial year a banking company (section 1164(2))`)
               , `s 474 was at some time within the financial year an e-money issuer`
               , `s 474 was at some time within the financial year a MiFID investment firm`
               , `s 474 was at some time within the financial year a UCITS management company`
               , (JUST `was at some time within the financial year carrying on insurance market activity (section 1165)`)
               , (JUST `was at some time within the financial year a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme within the meanings given by section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act (Northern Ireland) 2021`)
               , (JUST `was at some time within the financial year a special register body as defined in section 117(1) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992`)
               , (JUST `was at some time within the financial year an employers' association as defined in section 122 of that Act or Article 4 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992`)

§§ `s 479 Availability of small companies exemption in case of group company`

-- s 479(2) and s 479(5)(c) to (e) are shown blank in the text (coverage table: repealed or blank).

-- src:6598 | (a) “group company” means a company that is a parent company or a subsidiary undertaking, and
@ref s 479(4)(a) "group company" (src:6598-6598)
GIVEN `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1162 the company is a subsidiary undertaking` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 479(4)(a) the company is a group company` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF    `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `s 1162 the company is a subsidiary undertaking` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF    `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
          AND `s 1162 the company is a subsidiary undertaking` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“group company” means a company that is a parent company or a subsidiary undertaking"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "parent company" (section 1173(1)) or "subsidiary undertaking" (section 1162) is not known

-- src:6599 | (b) “the group”, in relation to a group company, means that company together with all its associated undertakings.
-- src:6600 | For this purpose undertakings are associated if one is a subsidiary undertaking of the other or both are subsidiary undertakings of a third undertaking.
@ref s 479(4)(b) "the group"; associated undertakings (src:6599-6600)
GIVEN `one is a subsidiary undertaking of the other` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `both are subsidiary undertakings of a third undertaking` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 479(4) the two undertakings are associated` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `one is a subsidiary undertaking of the other` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `both are subsidiary undertakings of a third undertaking` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `one is a subsidiary undertaking of the other` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `both are subsidiary undertakings of a third undertaking` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "undertakings are associated if one is a subsidiary undertaking of the other or both are subsidiary undertakings of a third undertaking" (an if read as the definition: fork F9)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subsidiary undertaking" (section 1162) is not known

-- src:6599 | (b) “the group”, in relation to a group company, means that company together with all its associated undertakings.
-- src:6600 | For this purpose undertakings are associated if one is a subsidiary undertaking of the other or both are subsidiary undertakings of a third undertaking.
@ref s 479(4)(b) "the group"; associated undertakings (src:6599-6600)
GIVEN `the undertaking is the group company itself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking is associated with the group company (section 479(4))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 479(4)(b) the undertaking belongs to the group of the group company` MEANS
    IF `the undertaking is the group company itself`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE `the undertaking is associated with the group company (section 479(4))` -- “the group” ... means that company together with all its associated undertakings: JUST FALSE is the text's no (it means), NOTHING stays NOTHING

-- src:6607 | (6) The provisions mentioned in subsection (5) apply for the purposes of this section as if all the bodies corporate in the group were companies.
@ref s 479(6) As if all the bodies corporate in the group were companies (src:6607-6607)
GIVEN `the body is a body corporate in the group` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 479(6) the body is treated as a company for the purposes of section 479(5)` MEANS
    IF `the body is a body corporate in the group`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as if all the bodies corporate in the group were companies" says nothing of a body outside the group

-- src:6596 | (3) A company is not excluded by subsection (1) if, throughout the whole of the period or periods during the financial year when it was a group company, it was both a subsidiary undertaking and dormant.
@ref s 479(3) A company is not excluded by subsection (1) if (src:6596-6596)
GIVEN `throughout the whole of the period or periods when it was a group company it was a subsidiary undertaking` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `throughout the whole of the period or periods when it was a group company it was dormant` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 479(3) subsection (3) applies: the company is not excluded by subsection (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF    `throughout the whole of the period or periods when it was a group company it was a subsidiary undertaking` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          AND `throughout the whole of the period or periods when it was a group company it was dormant` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF    `throughout the whole of the period or periods when it was a group company it was a subsidiary undertaking` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           OR `throughout the whole of the period or periods when it was a group company it was dormant` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is not excluded by subsection (1) if, throughout the whole of the period or periods during the financial year when it was a group company, it was both a subsidiary undertaking and dormant": the if is not met, so subsection (3) does not apply (an if read clause by clause: fork F10)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subsidiary undertaking" (section 1162) or "dormant" (section 1169) is not known

-- src:6590 | (1) A company is not entitled to the exemption conferred by section 477 (small companies) in respect of a financial year during any part of which it was a group company unless—
-- src:6591 | (a) the group—
-- src:6592 | (i) qualifies as a small group in relation to that financial year, and
-- src:6593 | (ii) was not at any time in that year an ineligible group, or
-- src:6594 | (b) subsection (3) applies.
@ref s 479(1) Not entitled in respect of a financial year during any part of which it was a group company unless (src:6590-6594)
GIVEN `the company was a group company during any part of the financial year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 383 the group qualifies as a small group in relation to the financial year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 384(2) and (3) the group was at some time in the year an ineligible group` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 479(3) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 479(1) the company is barred from the small companies exemption as a group company` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the company was a group company during any part of the financial year` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in respect of a financial year during any part of which it was a group company": the bar reaches only a group company
        IF `section 479(3) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) subsection (3) applies" (the unless is met: fork F3)
        IF    `s 383 the group qualifies as a small group in relation to the financial year` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          AND `s 384(2) and (3) the group was at some time in the year an ineligible group` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless— (a) the group— (i) qualifies as a small group in relation to that financial year, and (ii) was not at any time in that year an ineligible group" (the unless is met: fork F3)
        IF    `the company was a group company during any part of the financial year` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          AND `section 479(3) applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
          AND (    `s 383 the group qualifies as a small group in relation to the financial year` EQUALS JUST FALSE
                OR `s 384(2) and (3) the group was at some time in the year an ineligible group` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE -- "A company is not entitled to the exemption conferred by section 477 ... unless" neither limb of (a) nor (b) holds
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 383, section 384(2) and (3) or "group company" (section 479(4)) is not known

§§ `s 479A Subsidiary companies: conditions for exemption from audit`

-- src:6610 | (1) A company is exempt from the requirements of this Act relating to the audit of individual accounts for a financial year if—
-- src:6611 | (a) it is itself a subsidiary undertaking, and
-- src:6612 | (b) its parent undertaking is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom.
@ref s 479A(1) A subsidiary company is exempt from audit of its individual accounts if (src:6610-6612)
GIVEN `the company is itself a subsidiary undertaking (section 1162)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its parent undertaking is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 479A(1) the company is within the subsidiary companies audit exemption` MEANS
    IF `the company is itself a subsidiary undertaking (section 1162)` AND `its parent undertaking is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is exempt from the requirements of this Act relating to the audit of individual accounts for a financial year if— (a) it is itself a subsidiary undertaking, and (b) its parent undertaking is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom": this section gives no exemption on these facts (fork F1)

-- src:6620 | (e) the directors of the company must deliver to the registrar on or before the date that they file the accounts for that year—
-- src:6621 | (i) a written notice of the agreement referred to in subsection (2)(a),
-- src:6622 | (ii) the statement referred to in section 479C(1),
-- src:6623 | (iii) a copy of the consolidated accounts referred to in subsection (2)(c),
-- src:6624 | (iv) a copy of the auditor's report on those accounts, and
-- src:6625 | (v) a copy of the consolidated annual report drawn up by the parent undertaking.
@ref s 479A(2)(e) The directors must deliver to the registrar on or before the date they file the accounts (src:6620-6625)
DECLARE `s 479A(2)(e) documents delivered to the registrar` HAS
    `s 479A(2)(e) the date the directors file the accounts for the year` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `s 479A(2)(e)(i) the date the written notice of the agreement was delivered` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `s 479A(2)(e)(ii) the date the statement referred to in section 479C(1) was delivered` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `s 479A(2)(e)(iii) the date the copy of the consolidated accounts was delivered` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `s 479A(2)(e)(iv) the date the copy of the auditor's report on those accounts was delivered` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `s 479A(2)(e)(v) the date the copy of the consolidated annual report was delivered` IS A MAYBE DATE

-- src:6620 | (e) the directors of the company must deliver to the registrar on or before the date that they file the accounts for that year—
-- src:6621 | (i) a written notice of the agreement referred to in subsection (2)(a),
-- src:6622 | (ii) the statement referred to in section 479C(1),
-- src:6623 | (iii) a copy of the consolidated accounts referred to in subsection (2)(c),
-- src:6624 | (iv) a copy of the auditor's report on those accounts, and
-- src:6625 | (v) a copy of the consolidated annual report drawn up by the parent undertaking.
@ref s 479A(2)(e) The directors must deliver to the registrar on or before the date they file the accounts (src:6620-6625)
GIVEN `filing date` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date delivered` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 479A(2)(e) one document was delivered on or before the date the directors file the accounts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `filing date`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on or before the date that they file the accounts for that year": the accounts have not been filed, so the date has not come
    WHEN JUST filed THEN
        CONSIDER `date delivered`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the directors of the company must deliver to the registrar on or before the date that they file the accounts": nothing delivered by the filing date
        WHEN JUST delivered THEN
            IF delivered AT MOST filed
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on or before the date that they file the accounts for that year": delivered after that date

-- src:6620 | (e) the directors of the company must deliver to the registrar on or before the date that they file the accounts for that year—
-- src:6621 | (i) a written notice of the agreement referred to in subsection (2)(a),
-- src:6622 | (ii) the statement referred to in section 479C(1),
-- src:6623 | (iii) a copy of the consolidated accounts referred to in subsection (2)(c),
-- src:6624 | (iv) a copy of the auditor's report on those accounts, and
-- src:6625 | (v) a copy of the consolidated annual report drawn up by the parent undertaking.
@ref s 479A(2)(e) The directors must deliver to the registrar on or before the date they file the accounts (src:6620-6625)
GIVEN documents IS A `s 479A(2)(e) documents delivered to the registrar`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 479A(2)(e) the five documents were delivered on or before the date the directors file the accounts` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN limb YIELD limb EQUALS JUST FALSE) limbs
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the directors of the company must deliver to the registrar on or before the date that they file the accounts for that year— (i) ... (v)": a document was not delivered, or was delivered late
        IF all (GIVEN limb YIELD limb EQUALS JUST TRUE) limbs THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on or before the date that they file the accounts for that year": the accounts have not been filed, so the date has not come
    WHERE
        filed MEANS documents's `s 479A(2)(e) the date the directors file the accounts for the year`
        limbs MEANS
            LIST `s 479A(2)(e) one document was delivered on or before the date the directors file the accounts` filed (documents's `s 479A(2)(e)(i) the date the written notice of the agreement was delivered`)
               , `s 479A(2)(e) one document was delivered on or before the date the directors file the accounts` filed (documents's `s 479A(2)(e)(ii) the date the statement referred to in section 479C(1) was delivered`)
               , `s 479A(2)(e) one document was delivered on or before the date the directors file the accounts` filed (documents's `s 479A(2)(e)(iii) the date the copy of the consolidated accounts was delivered`)
               , `s 479A(2)(e) one document was delivered on or before the date the directors file the accounts` filed (documents's `s 479A(2)(e)(iv) the date the copy of the auditor's report on those accounts was delivered`)
               , `s 479A(2)(e) one document was delivered on or before the date the directors file the accounts` filed (documents's `s 479A(2)(e)(v) the date the copy of the consolidated annual report was delivered`)

-- src:6613 | (2) Exemption is conditional upon compliance with all of the following conditions—
-- src:6614 | (a) all members of the company must agree to the exemption in respect of the financial year in question,
-- src:6615 | (b) the parent undertaking must give a guarantee under section 479C in respect of that year,
-- src:6616 | (c) the company must be included in the consolidated accounts drawn up for that year or to an earlier date in that year by the parent undertaking in accordance with—
-- src:6617 | (i) if the undertaking is a company, the requirements of Part 15 of this Act, or, if the undertaking is not a company, the legal requirements which apply to the drawing up of consolidated accounts for that undertaking, or
-- src:6618 | (ii) UK-adopted international accounting standards (within the meaning given by section 474(1)),
-- src:6619 | (d) the parent undertaking must disclose in the notes to the consolidated accounts that the company is exempt from the requirements of this Act relating to the audit of individual accounts by virtue of this section, and
-- src:6620 | (e) the directors of the company must deliver to the registrar on or before the date that they file the accounts for that year—
-- src:6621 | (i) a written notice of the agreement referred to in subsection (2)(a),
-- src:6622 | (ii) the statement referred to in section 479C(1),
-- src:6623 | (iii) a copy of the consolidated accounts referred to in subsection (2)(c),
-- src:6624 | (iv) a copy of the auditor's report on those accounts, and
-- src:6625 | (v) a copy of the consolidated annual report drawn up by the parent undertaking.
@ref s 479A(2) Exemption is conditional upon compliance with all of the following conditions (src:6613-6625)
GIVEN `all members of the company agree to the exemption in respect of the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parent undertaking has given a guarantee under section 479C in respect of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is included in the consolidated accounts drawn up for the year or to an earlier date in the year by the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parent undertaking is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those consolidated accounts were drawn up in accordance with the requirements of Part 15` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those consolidated accounts were drawn up in accordance with the legal requirements which apply to the drawing up of consolidated accounts for that undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those consolidated accounts were drawn up in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards (within the meaning given by section 474(1))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parent undertaking discloses in the notes to the consolidated accounts that the company is exempt by virtue of section 479A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 479A(2)(e) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 479A(2) the conditions of the exemption are complied with` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF    (NOT `all members of the company agree to the exemption in respect of the financial year`)
           OR (NOT `the parent undertaking has given a guarantee under section 479C in respect of the year`)
           OR (NOT `the company is included in the consolidated accounts drawn up for the year or to an earlier date in the year by the parent undertaking`)
           OR (NOT `the consolidated accounts meet the (c) standard`)
           OR (NOT `the parent undertaking discloses in the notes to the consolidated accounts that the company is exempt by virtue of section 479A`)
           OR `section 479A(2)(e) answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Exemption is conditional upon compliance with all of the following conditions"
        IF `section 479A(2)(e) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (e) is not yet decidable (the accounts have not been filed)
    WHERE
        `the consolidated accounts meet the (c) standard` MEANS
            IF `the parent undertaking is a company`
            THEN `those consolidated accounts were drawn up in accordance with the requirements of Part 15` OR `those consolidated accounts were drawn up in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards (within the meaning given by section 474(1))`
            ELSE `those consolidated accounts were drawn up in accordance with the legal requirements which apply to the drawing up of consolidated accounts for that undertaking` OR `those consolidated accounts were drawn up in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards (within the meaning given by section 474(1))`

-- src:6626 | (3) This section has effect subject to—
-- src:6627 | section 475(2) and (3) (requirements as to statements contained in balance sheet), and
-- src:6628 | section 476 (right of members to require audit).
@ref s 479A(3) This section has effect subject to section 475(2) and (3) and section 476 (src:6626-6628)
GIVEN `section 479A(1) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 479A(2) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 479B answer (BAR polarity)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 475(2) answer (BAR polarity)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 475(3) answer (BAR polarity)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 475(4) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a valid notice under section 476 has been given` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 479A(3) the company is entitled to the exemption conferred by section 479A` MEANS
    `s 475(2) to (4) the exemption is in force once the restrictions on it are taken together`
        own
        (LIST `section 479B answer (BAR polarity)`, `section 475(2) answer (BAR polarity)`, `section 475(3) answer (BAR polarity)`, `a valid notice under section 476 has been given`)
        `section 475(4) answer`
    WHERE
        -- the exemption's own conditions: subsection (1) and every condition of subsection (2) ("Exemption is conditional upon compliance with all of the following conditions")
        own MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `section 479A(1) answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `section 479A(2) answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Exemption is conditional upon compliance with all of the following conditions" and "is exempt ... if": this section gives no exemption on these facts (internal: the exemption's own conditions, fork F1)
                IF `section 479A(1) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `section 479A(2) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
                OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer for subsection (1) or (2) is not known

§§ `s 479B Companies excluded from the subsidiary companies audit exemption`

-- src:6629 | 479B Companies excluded from the subsidiary companies audit exemption
-- src:6630 | A company is not entitled to the exemption conferred by section 479A (subsidiary companies) if it was at any time within the financial year in question—
-- src:6631 | (a) a traded company as defined in section 474(1),
-- src:6632 | (b) a company that—
-- src:6633 | (i) is an authorised insurance company, a banking company, an e-money issuer, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company, or
-- src:6634 | (ii) carries on insurance market activity, or
-- src:6635 | (iii) is a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme within the meanings given by section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act (Northern Ireland) 2021 (interpretation of Part 1), or
-- src:6636 | (c) a special register body as defined in section 117(1) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (c 52) or an employers' association as defined in section 122 of that Act or Article 4 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992 (S.I. 1992/807) (NI 5).
@ref s 479B Companies excluded from the subsidiary companies audit exemption (src:6629-6636)
GIVEN `s 474(1) was at some time within the financial year a traded company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `was at some time within the financial year an authorised insurance company (section 1165(2))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was at some time within the financial year a banking company (section 1164(2))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 474 was at some time within the financial year an e-money issuer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 474 was at some time within the financial year a MiFID investment firm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 474 was at some time within the financial year a UCITS management company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `was at some time within the financial year carrying on insurance market activity (section 1165)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was at some time within the financial year a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme within the meanings given by section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act (Northern Ireland) 2021` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was at some time within the financial year a special register body as defined in section 117(1) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was at some time within the financial year an employers' association as defined in section 122 of that Act or Article 4 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 479B the company is barred from the subsidiary companies audit exemption` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN limb YIELD limb EQUALS JUST TRUE) limbs THEN JUST TRUE -- "A company is not entitled to the exemption conferred by section 479A (subsidiary companies) if it was at any time within the financial year in question"
        IF all (GIVEN limb YIELD limb EQUALS JUST FALSE) limbs
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not entitled to the exemption conferred by section 479A (subsidiary companies) if it was at any time within the financial year in question— (a) a traded company ..., (b) a company that ..., or (c) a special register body": no listed kind holds, so this section does not bar it (fork F8)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a borrowed definition (traded company, e-money issuer, MiFID investment firm, UCITS management company: section 474(1)) is not known
    WHERE
        limbs MEANS
            LIST `s 474(1) was at some time within the financial year a traded company`
               , (JUST `was at some time within the financial year an authorised insurance company (section 1165(2))`)
               , (JUST `was at some time within the financial year a banking company (section 1164(2))`)
               , `s 474 was at some time within the financial year an e-money issuer`
               , `s 474 was at some time within the financial year a MiFID investment firm`
               , `s 474 was at some time within the financial year a UCITS management company`
               , (JUST `was at some time within the financial year carrying on insurance market activity (section 1165)`)
               , (JUST `was at some time within the financial year a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme within the meanings given by section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act (Northern Ireland) 2021`)
               , (JUST `was at some time within the financial year a special register body as defined in section 117(1) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992`)
               , (JUST `was at some time within the financial year an employers' association as defined in section 122 of that Act or Article 4 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992`)

§§ `s 479C Subsidiary companies audit exemption: parent undertaking declaration of guarantee`

-- src:6638 | (1) A guarantee is given by a parent undertaking under this section when the directors of the subsidiary company deliver to the registrar a statement by the parent undertaking that it guarantees the subsidiary company under this section.
@ref s 479C(1) When a guarantee is given (src:6638-6638)
GIVEN `the directors of the subsidiary company have delivered a statement to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is a statement by the parent undertaking that it guarantees the subsidiary company under section 479C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 479C(1) a guarantee is given by the parent undertaking` MEANS
    IF    `the directors of the subsidiary company have delivered a statement to the registrar`
      AND `the statement is a statement by the parent undertaking that it guarantees the subsidiary company under section 479C`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A guarantee is given by a parent undertaking under this section when the directors of the subsidiary company deliver to the registrar a statement by the parent undertaking that it guarantees the subsidiary company under this section" ("when" counts as "where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (c); fork F11)

-- src:6639 | (2) The statement under subsection (1) must be authenticated by the parent undertaking and must specify—
-- src:6640 | (a) the name of the parent undertaking,
-- src:6641 | (b) the registered number (if any) of the parent undertaking,
-- src:6642 | (c) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:6643 | (d) the name and registered number of the subsidiary company in respect of which the guarantee is being given,
-- src:6644 | (e) the date of the statement, and
-- src:6645 | (f) the financial year to which the guarantee relates.
@ref s 479C(2) The statement must be authenticated and must specify (src:6639-6645)
GIVEN `the statement is authenticated by the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parent undertaking has a registered number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement specifies the name of the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement specifies the registered number of the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement specifies the name and registered number of the subsidiary company in respect of which the guarantee is being given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement specifies the date of the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement specifies the financial year to which the guarantee relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 479C(2) the statement meets the requirements` MEANS
    IF    `the statement is authenticated by the parent undertaking`
      AND `the statement specifies the name of the parent undertaking`
      AND (    (NOT `the parent undertaking has a registered number`)
            OR `the statement specifies the registered number of the parent undertaking`)
      AND `the statement specifies the name and registered number of the subsidiary company in respect of which the guarantee is being given`
      AND `the statement specifies the date of the statement`
      AND `the statement specifies the financial year to which the guarantee relates`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement under subsection (1) must be authenticated by the parent undertaking and must specify" (a bare must not done: fork F4); paragraph (b) says "(if any)", so a parent with no registered number need not specify one

-- src:6647 | (a) the parent undertaking guarantees all outstanding liabilities to which the subsidiary company is subject at the end of the financial year to which the guarantee relates, until they are satisfied in full, and
@ref s 479C(3)(a) The parent undertaking guarantees all outstanding liabilities (src:6647-6647)
GIVEN `the guarantee has been given under section 479C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability is one to which the subsidiary company is subject at the end of the financial year to which the guarantee relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability has been satisfied in full` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 479C(3)(a) the parent undertaking guarantees the liability` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the guarantee has been given under section 479C`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A guarantee given under this section has the effect that" says nothing where no guarantee is given
        IF NOT `the liability is one to which the subsidiary company is subject at the end of the financial year to which the guarantee relates`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "all outstanding liabilities to which the subsidiary company is subject at the end of the financial year to which the guarantee relates"
        IF `the liability has been satisfied in full`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until they are satisfied in full"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:6648 | (b) the guarantee is enforceable against the parent undertaking by any person to whom the subsidiary company is liable in respect of those liabilities.
@ref s 479C(3)(b) The guarantee is enforceable by any person to whom the subsidiary company is liable (src:6648-6648)
GIVEN `the guarantee has been given under section 479C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsidiary company is liable to the person in respect of those liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 479C(3)(b) the person may enforce the guarantee against the parent undertaking` MEANS
    IF `the guarantee has been given under section 479C` AND `the subsidiary company is liable to the person in respect of those liabilities`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "enforceable against the parent undertaking by any person to whom the subsidiary company is liable in respect of those liabilities" says nothing of anyone else

§§ `s 480 Dormant companies: conditions for exemption from audit`

-- src:6654 | (2) The conditions are that the company—
-- src:6655 | (a) as regards its individual accounts for the financial year in question—
-- src:6656 | (i) is entitled to prepare accounts in accordance with the small companies regime (see sections 381 to 384), or
-- src:6657 | (ii) would be so entitled but for having been a public company or a member of an ineligible group, and
-- src:6658 | (b) is not required to prepare group accounts for that year.
@ref s 480(2) The conditions (src:6654-6658)
GIVEN `s 381 the company is entitled to prepare accounts in accordance with the small companies regime as regards its individual accounts for the financial year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company would be so entitled but for having been a public company or a member of an ineligible group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is required to prepare group accounts for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 480(2) the conditions for the dormant companies exemption are met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the company is required to prepare group accounts for the year`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions are that the company— ... (b) is not required to prepare group accounts for that year"
        IF `s 381 the company is entitled to prepare accounts in accordance with the small companies regime as regards its individual accounts for the financial year` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the company would be so entitled but for having been a public company or a member of an ineligible group`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 381 the company is entitled to prepare accounts in accordance with the small companies regime as regards its individual accounts for the financial year` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions are that the company— (a) as regards its individual accounts for the financial year in question— (i) is entitled to prepare accounts in accordance with the small companies regime ..., or (ii) would be so entitled but for having been a public company or a member of an ineligible group"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): entitlement to the small companies regime (sections 381 to 384) is not known

-- src:6651 | (1) A company is exempt from the requirements of this Act relating to the audit of accounts in respect of a financial year if—
-- src:6652 | (a) it has been dormant since its formation, or
-- src:6653 | (b) it has been dormant since the end of the previous financial year and the following conditions are met.
@ref s 480(1) A dormant company is exempt from audit if (src:6651-6653)
GIVEN `s 1169(1) the company has been dormant since its formation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1169(1) the company has been dormant since the end of the previous financial year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 480(2) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 480(1) the company is exempt from audit under section 480` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 1169(1) the company has been dormant since its formation` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 1169(1) the company has been dormant since the end of the previous financial year` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `section 480(2) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF    `s 1169(1) the company has been dormant since its formation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
          AND (    `s 1169(1) the company has been dormant since the end of the previous financial year` EQUALS JUST FALSE
                OR `section 480(2) answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is exempt from the requirements of this Act relating to the audit of accounts in respect of a financial year if— (a) it has been dormant since its formation, or (b) it has been dormant since the end of the previous financial year and the following conditions are met": this section gives no exemption on these facts (fork F1)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): dormancy (section 1169) or the conditions of subsection (2) are not known

-- src:6659 | (3) This section has effect subject to—
-- src:6660 | section 475(2) and (3) (requirements as to statements to be contained in balance sheet),
-- src:6661 | section 476 (right of members to require audit), and
-- src:6662 | section 481 (companies excluded from dormant companies exemption).
@ref s 480(3) This section has effect subject to section 475(2) and (3), section 476 and section 481 (src:6659-6662)
GIVEN `section 480(1) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 481 answer (BAR polarity)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 475(2) answer (BAR polarity)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 475(3) answer (BAR polarity)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 475(4) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a valid notice under section 476 has been given` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 480(3) the company is entitled to the exemption conferred by section 480` MEANS
    `s 475(2) to (4) the exemption is in force once the restrictions on it are taken together`
        `section 480(1) answer`
        (LIST `section 481 answer (BAR polarity)`, `section 475(2) answer (BAR polarity)`, `section 475(3) answer (BAR polarity)`, `a valid notice under section 476 has been given`)
        `section 475(4) answer`

§§ `s 481 Companies excluded from dormant companies exemption`

-- src:6663 | 481 Companies excluded from dormant companies exemption
-- src:6664 | A company is not entitled to the exemption conferred by section 480 (dormant companies) if it was at any time within the financial year in question a company that—
-- src:6665 | (za) is a traded company as defined in section 474(1),
-- src:6666 | (a) is an authorised insurance company, a banking company, an e-money issuer, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company, or
-- src:6667 | (b) carries on insurance market activity.
@ref s 481 Companies excluded from dormant companies exemption (src:6663-6667)
GIVEN `s 474(1) was at some time within the financial year a traded company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `was at some time within the financial year an authorised insurance company (section 1165(2))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was at some time within the financial year a banking company (section 1164(2))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 474 was at some time within the financial year an e-money issuer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 474 was at some time within the financial year a MiFID investment firm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 474 was at some time within the financial year a UCITS management company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `was at some time within the financial year carrying on insurance market activity (section 1165)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 481 the company is barred from the dormant companies exemption` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN limb YIELD limb EQUALS JUST TRUE) limbs THEN JUST TRUE -- "A company is not entitled to the exemption conferred by section 480 (dormant companies) if it was at any time within the financial year in question a company that"
        IF all (GIVEN limb YIELD limb EQUALS JUST FALSE) limbs
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not entitled to the exemption conferred by section 480 (dormant companies) if it was at any time within the financial year in question a company that— (za) is a traded company ..., (a) is an authorised insurance company, ..., or (b) carries on insurance market activity": no listed kind holds, so this section does not bar it (fork F8)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a borrowed definition (traded company, e-money issuer, MiFID investment firm, UCITS management company: section 474(1)) is not known
    WHERE
        limbs MEANS
            LIST `s 474(1) was at some time within the financial year a traded company`
               , (JUST `was at some time within the financial year an authorised insurance company (section 1165(2))`)
               , (JUST `was at some time within the financial year a banking company (section 1164(2))`)
               , `s 474 was at some time within the financial year an e-money issuer`
               , `s 474 was at some time within the financial year a MiFID investment firm`
               , `s 474 was at some time within the financial year a UCITS management company`
               , (JUST `was at some time within the financial year carrying on insurance market activity (section 1165)`)

§§ `s 482 Non-profit-making companies subject to public sector audit`

-- src:6671 | (a) are subject to audit by the Comptroller and Auditor General by virtue of an order under section 25(6) of the Government Resources and Accounts Act 2000;
-- src:6672 | (ab) are subject to audit by the Auditor General for Wales by virtue of—
-- src:6673 | (i) an order under section 144 of the Government of Wales Act 1998, or
-- src:6674 | (ii) paragraph 18 of Schedule 8 to the Government of Wales Act 2006;
-- src:6675 | (b) are accounts—
-- src:6676 | (i) in relation to which section 21 of the Public Finance and Accountability (Scotland) Act 2000 (asp 1) (audit of accounts: Auditor General for Scotland) applies, or
-- src:6677 | (ii) that are subject to audit by the Auditor General for Scotland by virtue of an order under section 483 (Scottish public sector companies: audit by Auditor General for Scotland); or
-- src:6678 | (c) are subject to audit by the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland by virtue of an order under Article 5(3) of the Audit and Accountability (Northern Ireland) Order 2003 (S.I. 2003/418 (N.I. 5)).
@ref s 482(1) The routes of public sector audit (src:6671-6678)
DECLARE `s 482(1) route of public sector audit` IS ONE OF
    `s 482(1)(a) audit by the Comptroller and Auditor General by virtue of an order under section 25(6) of the Government Resources and Accounts Act 2000`
    `s 482(1)(ab)(i) audit by the Auditor General for Wales by virtue of an order under section 144 of the Government of Wales Act 1998`
    `s 482(1)(ab)(ii) audit by the Auditor General for Wales by virtue of paragraph 18 of Schedule 8 to the Government of Wales Act 2006`
    `s 482(1)(b)(i) accounts to which section 21 of the Public Finance and Accountability (Scotland) Act 2000 applies`
    `s 482(1)(b)(ii) audit by the Auditor General for Scotland by virtue of an order under section 483`
    `s 482(1)(c) audit by the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland by virtue of an order under Article 5(3) of the Audit and Accountability (Northern Ireland) Order 2003`
    `s 482(1) none of these routes`

-- src:6670 | (1) The requirements of this Part as to audit of accounts do not apply to a company for a financial year if it is non-profit-making and its accounts—
-- src:6671 | (a) are subject to audit by the Comptroller and Auditor General by virtue of an order under section 25(6) of the Government Resources and Accounts Act 2000;
-- src:6672 | (ab) are subject to audit by the Auditor General for Wales by virtue of—
-- src:6673 | (i) an order under section 144 of the Government of Wales Act 1998, or
-- src:6674 | (ii) paragraph 18 of Schedule 8 to the Government of Wales Act 2006;
-- src:6675 | (b) are accounts—
-- src:6676 | (i) in relation to which section 21 of the Public Finance and Accountability (Scotland) Act 2000 (asp 1) (audit of accounts: Auditor General for Scotland) applies, or
-- src:6677 | (ii) that are subject to audit by the Auditor General for Scotland by virtue of an order under section 483 (Scottish public sector companies: audit by Auditor General for Scotland); or
-- src:6678 | (c) are subject to audit by the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland by virtue of an order under Article 5(3) of the Audit and Accountability (Northern Ireland) Order 2003 (S.I. 2003/418 (N.I. 5)).
-- src:6679 | (2) In the case of a company that is a parent company or a subsidiary undertaking, subsection (1) applies only if every group undertaking is non-profit-making.
-- src:6680 | (3) In this section “non-profit-making” has the same meaning as in Article 54 of the Treaty on the Functioning of the European Union.
@ref s 482(1) to (3) Non-profit-making companies subject to public sector audit (src:6670-6680)
GIVEN route IS A `s 482(1) route of public sector audit`
      `the company is non-profit-making (Article 54 of the Treaty on the Functioning of the European Union)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a parent company or a subsidiary undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every group undertaking is non-profit-making` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 482(1) the requirements of Part 16 as to audit of accounts do not apply to the company` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the company is non-profit-making (Article 54 of the Treaty on the Functioning of the European Union)`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply to a company for a financial year if it is non-profit-making and its accounts": this section gives no exemption on these facts (fork F1)
        IF route EQUALS `s 482(1) none of these routes`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is non-profit-making and its accounts— (a) ... (ab) ... (b) ... or (c)": none of the listed routes holds
        IF `the company is a parent company or a subsidiary undertaking` AND (NOT `every group undertaking is non-profit-making`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection (1) applies only if every group undertaking is non-profit-making"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:6681 | (4) This section has effect subject to section 475(2) (balance sheet to contain statement that company entitled to exemption under this section).
@ref s 482(4) Subject to section 475(2) (src:6681-6681)
GIVEN `section 482(1) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 475(2) answer (BAR polarity)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 475(4) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 482(4) the company is entitled to the exemption conferred by section 482` MEANS
    `s 475(2) to (4) the exemption is in force once the restrictions on it are taken together`
        `section 482(1) answer`
        (LIST `section 475(2) answer (BAR polarity)`)
        `section 475(4) answer`

§§ `s 483 Scottish public sector companies: audit by Auditor General for Scotland`

-- The power of the Scottish Ministers is encoded for what it decides (when an order may be made and when it may not yet be
-- made), because an order is what puts a company within s 482(1)(b)(ii).  s 483(4), the scope of the order, is machinery.

-- src:6683 | (1) The Scottish Ministers may by order provide for the accounts of a company having its registered office in Scotland to be audited by the Auditor General for Scotland.
-- src:6684 | (2) An order under subsection (1) may be made in relation to a company only if it appears to the Scottish Ministers that the company—
-- src:6685 | (a) exercises in or as regards Scotland functions of a public nature none of which relate to reserved matters (within the meaning of the Scotland Act 1998 (c. 46)), or
-- src:6686 | (b) is entirely or substantially funded from a body having accounts falling within paragraph (a) or (b) of subsection (3).
@ref s 483(1) and (2) The Scottish Ministers may by order provide (src:6683-6686)
GIVEN `the company has its registered office in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Scottish Ministers that the company exercises in or as regards Scotland functions of a public nature none of which relate to reserved matters (within the meaning of the Scotland Act 1998)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Scottish Ministers that the company is entirely or substantially funded from a body having accounts falling within paragraph (a) or (b) of subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 483(1) the Scottish Ministers may by order provide for the company's accounts to be audited by the Auditor General for Scotland` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the company has its registered office in Scotland`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a company having its registered office in Scotland"
        IF    `it appears to the Scottish Ministers that the company exercises in or as regards Scotland functions of a public nature none of which relate to reserved matters (within the meaning of the Scotland Act 1998)`
           OR `it appears to the Scottish Ministers that the company is entirely or substantially funded from a body having accounts falling within paragraph (a) or (b) of subsection (3)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An order under subsection (1) may be made in relation to a company only if it appears to the Scottish Ministers that the company"

-- src:6687 | (3) Those accounts are—
-- src:6688 | (a) accounts in relation to which section 21 of the Public Finance and Accountability (Scotland) Act 2000 (asp 1) (audit of accounts: Auditor General for Scotland) applies,
-- src:6689 | (b) accounts which are subject to audit by the Auditor General for Scotland by virtue of an order under this section.
@ref s 483(3) Those accounts are (src:6687-6689)
GIVEN `the accounts are accounts in relation to which section 21 of the Public Finance and Accountability (Scotland) Act 2000 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounts are subject to audit by the Auditor General for Scotland by virtue of an order under section 483` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 483(3) the accounts are accounts falling within paragraph (a) or (b) of subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF    `the accounts are accounts in relation to which section 21 of the Public Finance and Accountability (Scotland) Act 2000 applies`
       OR `the accounts are subject to audit by the Auditor General for Scotland by virtue of an order under section 483`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Those accounts are— (a) ..., (b) ..." closes with no "only" (fork F12)

-- src:6691 | (5) An order under subsection (1) shall not be made unless a draft of the statutory instrument containing it has been laid before, and approved by resolution of, the Scottish Parliament.
@ref s 483(5) An order shall not be made unless a draft has been laid before and approved (src:6691-6691)
GIVEN `a draft of the statutory instrument containing the order has been laid before the Scottish Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the draft has been approved by resolution of the Scottish Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 483(5) the order may not yet be made` MEANS
    IF `a draft of the statutory instrument containing the order has been laid before the Scottish Parliament` AND `the draft has been approved by resolution of the Scottish Parliament`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An order under subsection (1) shall not be made unless a draft of the statutory instrument containing it has been laid before, and approved by resolution of, the Scottish Parliament" (the unless is met: fork F3)
    ELSE JUST TRUE -- "shall not be made unless" the draft has been laid and approved

-- s 484 General power of amendment by regulations (ss 484(1) to (4)): machinery (a regulation-making power and the procedure
-- for it), inert under reason 2; no declaration.
